From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:28:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: an x86_64 Linux build on winemetal (the VM's)

MacNeutron's Direct3D 9 in the VM: mtld3d-unix builds for
x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, always on the winemetal facade. Its pages come
from winemetal's allocator (slots 153/154, memory the host maps too); a
32-bit process's first thunk marks it, and the facade then calls
winemetal's WoW64 table, whose memory lies below 2 GiB. No crash
reporter on Linux (Wine's and FEX's handle faults there), memory
statistics from /proc/self/statm and mallinfo2, no translation query.
The facade builds allow the dead code only macOS's window paths reach;
the test that names each slot's function is macOS-only.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
